# The committed pictures live here: golden/parity/screens/<volume>/<step>.png,
# one per screenshot step of the extended tour (SCHEMA.md §2.3).
#
# THE DIRECTORY IS THE CONVENTION; THE PICTURES ARE NOT HERE YET. The
# screenshot steps were written while the fixes they are meant to hold were
# still landing on other branches, and a baseline taken from a build that is
# about to change is a baseline of the wrong thing. So until the final capture
# wave runs `capture.mjs --capture-extended` against the finished build, a
# walk's pictures are a candidate with no twin and `compare.mjs` reports them
# as "not captured" rather than as a pass.
#
# THE FINAL WAVE DELETES THE LINE BELOW and commits the pictures it took. That
# is the whole of the switch: with pictures here the gate compares them, and
# with the extended steps in the baselines it walks them (compare.mjs,
# `extendedBaseline`).
*.png
